 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a cached preview is served (cache hit), the system SHALL promote its entry from the Am queue to the head of the A1 queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When the Am queue exceeds 3 GiB, the system SHALL evict entries from the tail of Am until it is within 3 GiB before considering A1 eviction.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When the A1 queue exceeds 9 GiB and the Am queue is within its 3 GiB target, the system SHALL evict entries from the tail of A1 until it is within 9 GiB.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When a new preview is admitted, the system SHALL place its entry at the head of the Am queue.
